/.claude/worktrees
.env
.env.migrate.*
scripts/jira/dist/
# where-are-we ledger L2: regenerated-from-live-sources cache, not
# source of truth — never commit it.
/.where-are-we/
# node_modules anywhere — none are tracked. A per-package list let
# marketplace/plugins/*/node_modules/ slip through and be sweepable.
node_modules/
/.claude/settings.local.json
# /allow-rule backups (.bak-<epoch>-<pid>) and mktemp orphans written beside it.
/.claude/settings.local.json.*
# tokensave MCP code-graph state (local SQLite DB, session-generated — never commit).
/.tokensave/
# graphify knowledge-graph artifacts: this repo's derived graph is not
# published, so the directory is ignored OUTRIGHT, nothing re-included.
# Working files stay on disk — the daily graph-map refresh cadence rebuilds
# them locally, and every place that would commit or PR the graph no-ops on
# this ignored path.
graphify-out/*
# .claudeignore
# graphify writes output files (graph.json, graphify-out/) into the workspace. Ignoring them keeps them out of file search and context. It is NOT a prompt-cache fix: a graph.json write does not invalidate a running session's prompt cache (measured: docs/internals/prompt-cache.md, eval no-invalidation). Add them to .claudeignore:
graph.json
graphify-out/
/.claude/skills/graphify/
# graphify multi-harness init scatters per-machine integration files across the
# repo. Regenerable via /graphify, same as the ignored skills dir
# above.
/.github/copilot-instructions.md
.agents/rules/graphify.md
.agents/workflows/graphify.md
# Generated/junk artifacts that must never be committed.
# NOT package-lock.json globally — 6 legit npm packages track theirs. The
# wrong-PM lockfile case (a package-lock.json inside a bun package, left by the
# npm-audit pre-push gates) is prevented per-bun-package via that package's own
# .gitignore (e.g. marketplace/plugins/luna-correlate/, scripts/luna-vitals/),
# and still backstopped by the check-artifact-leakage pre-commit hook.
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# stray empty scratch file at the repo root — not produced by any himmel script;
# anchored so it only ignores the root stray.
/.tmp
# end-session-wiki hook local artifacts — contain raw transcript excerpts (potential secrets).
# Match any .claude/ dir (the hook writes into the cwd's .claude/, e.g. scripts/telegram/.claude/).
**/.claude/end-session-wiki.log
**/.claude/end-session-wiki.log.old
# run-hook-with-bash.js --chain durable skip/deny log — local
# diagnostics, not source. Not root-anchored (CR round 4, codex-2): the
# launcher falls back to cwd when CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is unset, so a nested
# invocation writes .claude/logs/ under a subdirectory too.
**/.claude/logs/
# Handover transient state
.last-consolidate.json
**/handovers/*/.last-consolidate.json
.pending-new-item*
**/handovers/*/.pending-new-item*
.pending-consolidate*
**/handovers/*/.pending-consolidate*
# auto-arm-on-cap / auto-arm-on-subagent-cap runtime snapshots —
# the hooks write these into himmel handovers/ as untracked clutter on main.
# (Followup: redirect the hook write path to HANDOVER_DIR — see HIMMEL ticket.)
handovers/auto-arm-status-*.md
# arm-resume lock files (arms.jsonl) — transient arming-lock state that lands in
# the himmel handovers/ stub as untracked clutter; observed staged on main,
# same class as the auto-arm-status snapshots above.
handovers/.locks/
# Overnight-mode reports/recovery artifacts — auto-generated session state
# (morning-report.sh et al.) that belongs in the state repo, not the himmel
# handovers/ stub. Archived copies live in <state-repo> handovers/yotamleo/himmel/.
handovers/overnight-report-*.md
handovers/overnight-recovery-*.md
# Worker inbox + cursors: the one untracked subtree left in the
# primary's handovers/ stub that showed in every `git status`.
/handovers/inbox/
# Cross-project handover content lives in <state-repo>; these entries
# prevent re-tracking if the operator's local copy still exists or an
# out-of-date tool re-creates it here.
/handovers/luna/
/handovers/manual_notes.md
/handovers/random_dreams.md
# Runtime artifacts that pollute primary-worktree git status
.claire/
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# The settings writers' exclusive lock. Transient, but it sits
# beside a TRACKED file, so a crash-orphaned one would otherwise be swept up by
# `git add -A`.
/.claude/settings.json.lock
/.playwright-mcp
# Legacy /improve disk artifacts (command removed). Kept so a
# clone that still holds saved drafts never sweeps them up with `git add -A`.
/.improve/
# overnight-mode Mode A (no HANDOVER_DIR) regenerates plans under
# docs/superpowers/plans/ — keep those local, never track the folder into
# the public repo.
/docs/superpowers/
# Internal design/plan/decision specs belong in the luna state repo, never in
# himmel docs/. himmel docs/ is reference + OSS-public only. Ignore
# docs/specs/ so migrated-out specs can't silently re-track (and never leak to
# the public mirror). New specs go to <state-repo>/handovers/<user>/<repo>/specs/.
/docs/specs/
# Decision records (ADRs) are state-repo work artifacts too —
# they belong in <state-repo>/.../specs/decision/, never himmel docs/.
/docs/adr/
# Codex artifacts. The guardrail wiring is
# TRACKED (hooks.json + the run-hook wrapper + its README); codex's local
# runtime config, sessions, and auto-generated slash-command→skill mirrors stay
# ignored. (AGENTS.md itself is tracked separately.)
.codex/*
!.codex/hooks.json
!.codex/run-hook.sh
!.codex/codex-hook-adapter.sh
!.codex/README.md
.agents/skills/source-command-*/
# himmel-contributor marker (opt-in; enables doc-guard gate) — never commit it
.himmel-dev
# per-operator CR registry overlay (account quota state) — never commit
scripts/cr/critics.local.json
# per-machine lane availability/override overlay (himmelctl config) — never commit
scripts/lanes/lanes.local.json
# machine-local grok tool-schema cache dir — never commit
/mcps/
# scripts/lanes/bench/runs/: bench RUN-OUTPUT JSONs live in the luna state
# repo; the bench tooling still writes fresh runs here locally, so the
# directory is ignored. See scripts/lib/public-clone-paths.sh for why.
scripts/lanes/bench/runs/
# stray Corsair iCUE/CorsairLink driver log dropped in the repo root by the
# host tooling — machine-local noise, never ours to commit.
CorsairLink.log
# CPython bytecode for the harness's tracked .py sources — pure build
# byproducts, regenerated on the next import, never work product.
# Left untracked-but-unignored, they read to clean-garden as "untracked files
# that are not known strays (possible forgotten work)", so it correctly refuses
# to prune — and EVERY merged worktree became unprunable (5 of 5 on this
# station). The guard's verdict was right; the repo had just never told git
# these files are noise.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Vitest's own reporter output dir (any tracked `vitest run`
# invocation mints it), same class of noise as __pycache__ above.
.vitest/
# Two recurring strays that tripped himmel-update's dirty-tree
# gate before the gate was scoped to tracked changes — a `bun.lock` `bun
# install` drops inside the npm-managed scripts/bitbucket/, and a claude-hud
# plugin config the HUD writes locally. Both are pure noise, never ours to
# commit.
scripts/bitbucket/bun.lock
.claude/plugins/claude-hud/config.json
# Docs site build output
site/dist/
site/node_modules/
site/.astro/
